Package: ipeds
Type: Package
Title: Download, Label and Harmonize Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System (IPEDS) Data
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-09-29
Authors@R: c(
    person("Chris", "Birdsall", email = "ccbirdsall@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Jason", "Bryer", email = "jason@bryer.org", role = "aut",
           comment = "Original author of the ipeds package"))
URL: https://github.com/chrisbirdsall/ipeds
BugReports: https://github.com/chrisbirdsall/ipeds/issues
Description: The Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System (IPEDS) is the
    core postsecondary education data collection of the National Center for
    Education Statistics (NCES). This package downloads IPEDS complete data
    files directly from the NCES data center (preferring revised releases),
    caches them locally, attaches variable and value labels from the official
    data dictionaries, and builds institution-by-year panels in which
    measures are harmonized across changes in IPEDS definitions, such as the
    2008-2010 move to the new race/ethnicity categories, the 2010 retirement
    of first-professional and old doctoral award levels, the 2014 move of
    admissions data out of Institutional Characteristics, the 2016 SAT
    redesign, locale and Carnegie classification revisions, and
    parent/child reporting. Every harmonized variable is checked against the
    labels in the IPEDS dictionary for the file it came from and the results
    are recorded in an audit trail.
